1
00:00:03,590 --> 00:00:06,170
I'm telling you, if xenon emits ultraviolet light,

2
00:00:06,170 --> 00:00:08,560
then those dark matter discoveries must be wrong.

3
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:10,470
Yes, well, if we lived in a world

4
00:00:10,470 --> 00:00:12,380
where slow-moving xenon produced light,

5
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:13,430
then you'd be correct.

6
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:15,050
Also, pigs would fly,

7
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:17,500
my derriere would produce cotton candy,

8
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,270
and The Phantom Menace would be a timeless classic.

9
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:22,430
Oh, you're so arrogant.

10
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:23,420
If you were a superhero,

11
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:25,150
your name would be Captain Arrogant.

12
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,160
And you know what your superpower would be?

13
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,820
Arrogance.

14
00:00:29,610 --> 00:00:30,890
You're wrong again.

15
00:00:30,890 --> 00:00:32,670
If my superpower were arrogance,

16
00:00:32,670 --> 00:00:35,530
my name would be Dr. Arroganto.

17
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:40,310
I love watching Raj and Sheldon try to work together.

18
00:00:40,310 --> 00:00:42,520
Yeah, it's like if Alien and Predator decided

19
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,870
to go partners in a Jamba Juice.

20
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:47,610
Has it occurred to you you're missing the big picture?

21
00:00:47,610 --> 00:00:49,590
- If you look at neutron scattering data...  - Oh, Penny?

22
00:00:49,590 --> 00:00:50,590
- Penny?  - What's up?

23
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:53,730
Nothing. I just wanted to make Raj stop talking.

24
00:00:55,610 --> 00:00:56,350
No, no, no.

25
00:00:56,350 --> 00:00:58,300
He won. Suck it up.

26
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:00,570
Well, I'd ask you guys if you want dessert,

27
00:01:00,570 --> 00:01:02,480
but I know Sheldon doesn't eat dessert on Tuesdays.

28
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:05,300
And even if Raj wanted something, he couldn't tell me.

29
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:06,410
Howard won't order anything,

30
00:01:06,410 --> 00:01:08,370
but he will come up with some sort of skeevy comment

31
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:11,000
involving the words pie or cheesecake.

32
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,450
And Leonard's lactose intolerant,

33
00:01:12,450 --> 00:01:13,590
so he can't eat anything here

34
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:16,580
without his intestines blowing up like a balloon animal.

35
00:01:18,170 --> 00:01:19,220
Hang on a second.

36
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:20,800
I could have the fruit platter.

37
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:21,820
You want the fruit platter?

38
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:23,170
- Does it have melon on it?  - Yeah.

39
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:24,950
No, I can't eat melon.

40
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:27,420
Oh, Howard, heads up.

41
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:30,020
Your ex-girlfriend just came in for her shift.

42
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,770
When was the last time you saw her?

43
00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:34,190
Oh, not since we broke up.

44
00:01:34,190 --> 00:01:37,090
Wow. How am I going to play this?

45
00:01:37,090 --> 00:01:39,070
Sophisticated and relaxed?

46
00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:40,630
Friendly, noncommittal?

47
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:42,230
Cold and distant?

48
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:46,670
Hi, guys.

49
00:01:46,670 --> 00:01:48,560
Hello.

50
00:01:50,210 --> 00:01:53,640
I see you decided to go with pathetic and frightened.

51
00:01:54,050 --> 00:01:55,380
It's one of his best moves.

52
00:02:43,190 --> 00:02:46,310
So, my dear, we meet again.

53
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:49,930
Hello, Howard.

54
00:02:49,930 --> 00:02:51,410
I've missed you.

55
00:02:51,410 --> 00:02:54,640
I've missed you, Katee Sackhoff.

56
00:02:55,350 --> 00:02:57,690
- One question.  - Anything.

57
00:02:57,690 --> 00:03:01,300
Why am I wearing my Battlestar Galactica flight suit in bed?

58
00:03:01,570 --> 00:03:03,740
Why are you in bed with me?

59
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:07,100
If we start to question this, it all falls apart.

60
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,180
Sorry.

61
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:12,210
Oh, ravish me, Howard.

62
00:03:12,210 --> 00:03:14,510
My loins ache for you.

63
00:03:15,330 --> 00:03:17,600
Okay, if you insist.

64
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:21,900
Howard, have you seen my girdle?!

65
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:23,270
No, Ma!

66
00:03:23,270 --> 00:03:27,850
I can't find it, and I'm late for my Weight Watchers meeting!

67
00:03:27,850 --> 00:03:29,700
Maybe it committed suicide!

68
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:31,420
Leave me alone!

69
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:35,080
Now, where were we?

70
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:35,880
I believe you were about

71
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:38,630
to rip off my uniform with your teeth.

72
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:41,130
Bernadette?!

73
00:03:41,130 --> 00:03:42,700
What are you doing here?

74
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:44,530
Well, if I had to guess, I'd say I'm here

75
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:46,200
because you saw me earlier this evening,

76
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,500
and you're still hung up on me.

77
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,880
No, I'm not.

78
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:50,550
Clearly you are.

79
00:03:52,830 --> 00:03:55,260
Otherwise, based on past experience,

80
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:57,610
we'd be done by now.

81
00:03:59,050 --> 00:04:01,830
Okay, I'm a little confused here.

82
00:04:01,830 --> 00:04:04,670
Oh, my. Can I help?

83
00:04:07,010 --> 00:04:09,100
Not that kind of confused.

84
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:10,740
What's George Takei doing here?

85
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:13,380
Howard, do you have latent homosexual tendencies?

86
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:15,100
No, of course not.

87
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:16,810
So you say.

88
00:04:16,810 --> 00:04:19,420
Yet, here I am.

89
00:04:21,730 --> 00:04:23,540
George, let me ask you something.

90
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:26,780
How did you deal with being typecast as a science fiction icon?

91
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:27,890
It's difficult.

92
00:04:27,890 --> 00:04:29,990
You try and stretch as an actor--

93
00:04:29,990 --> 00:04:31,880
do Strindberg, O'Neill,

94
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:35,150
but all they want is, "Course laid in, Captain."

95
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:37,390
Tell me about it.

96
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:39,630
It's frackin' frustrating.

97
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:43,030
Wait. Katee, why are you leaving?

98
00:04:43,030 --> 00:04:46,210
She's leaving because you really want to be with me.

99
00:04:46,210 --> 00:04:49,070
Howard, I found my girdle!

100
00:04:49,070 --> 00:04:51,250
It was in the dryer!

101
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:52,410
Great, Ma!

102
00:04:52,410 --> 00:04:53,890
I think it shrunk!

103
00:04:53,890 --> 00:04:57,940
I'm spilling out like the Pillsbury Doughboy here!

104
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,330
And with that mental picture,

105
00:05:00,330 --> 00:05:03,130
I think we're done for the evening.

106
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:11,990
You never told me what happened between you and Bernadette.

107
00:05:11,990 --> 00:05:13,580
I did a stupid thing.

108
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:15,430
Yeah, I guessed that.

109
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:20,730
It was the kind of thing that makes it kind of hard to face her now.

110
00:05:20,730 --> 00:05:22,830
That covers anything from farting in bed

111
00:05:22,830 --> 00:05:25,010
to killing a homeless guy.

112
00:05:26,940 --> 00:05:27,620
Oh, my God.

113
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,860
You ran over a hobo.

114
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:31,770
No. Stop asking.

115
00:05:31,770 --> 00:05:33,890
All right, fine. So you want to get back together with her,

116
00:05:33,890 --> 00:05:35,290
but you're too ashamed to face her

117
00:05:35,290 --> 00:05:37,660
because of whatever it is you did.

118
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:38,950
- In a nutshell. - Okay.

119
00:05:38,950 --> 00:05:40,870
Well, how about this?

120
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:42,630
Kidnap Bernadette from the opera

121
00:05:42,630 --> 00:05:45,840
wearing a creepy mask so she doesn't know it's you.

122
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:50,220
Now, you see, I don't know if you're kidding or not.

123
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,410
You're being unreasonable.

124
00:05:52,410 --> 00:05:54,270
Why can't I have a desk?!

125
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:56,570
Our collaboration is a work of the mind.

126
00:05:56,570 --> 00:05:58,390
We don't need desks.

127
00:05:58,390 --> 00:05:59,570
You have a desk.

128
00:05:59,570 --> 00:06:01,190
- Correct. - But I can't have one.

129
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:02,930
You're two for two.

130
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,260
Why can't he have a desk, Sheldon?

131
00:06:05,260 --> 00:06:06,890
Oh, Lord, will this day never end?

132
00:06:06,890 --> 00:06:10,090
As I've explained repeatedly to Dr. Koothrappali,

133
00:06:10,090 --> 00:06:12,940
whose ability to comprehend the American idiom fails him

134
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:14,260
when it's convenient.

135
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:18,150
There's absolutely no money in my budget for additional office furniture.

136
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:20,780
Oh, but there's money for a drawer full of Red Vines,

137
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:22,570
a marshmallow shooting rifle,

138
00:06:22,570 --> 00:06:26,390
and a super executive ant farm with glow-in-the-dark sand?

139
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:29,550
Yes.

140
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:31,490
Okay, what if he buys his own desk?

141
00:06:31,490 --> 00:06:32,700
Yeah, what if I buy my own desk?

142
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:34,300
- That's ridiculous. - Why?

143
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:36,230
Because...

144
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:41,760
Yes?

145
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:44,050
It's my office.

146
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,760
- Sheldon. - All right, all right.

147
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:48,020
He can buy his own desk.

148
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:50,550
And I can put it in your office?

149
00:06:50,550 --> 00:06:54,360
Well, you really want to dot the I's and cross the T's, don't you?

150
00:06:54,730 --> 00:06:56,500
Why would you want a glow-in-the-dark ant farm?

151
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:59,030
They do some of their best work at night.

152
00:07:05,470 --> 00:07:07,490
Ah, it's okay.

153
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,870
Penny?

154
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:12,700
Penny?

155
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:13,810
Penny?

156
00:07:20,390 --> 00:07:22,300
Penny?

157
00:07:24,430 --> 00:07:26,560
Would you have opened the door if you knew it was me?

158
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,320
Not since I found out

159
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:30,320
the teddy bear you gave me had a webcam in it.

160
00:07:32,210 --> 00:07:33,700
I just have a question.

161
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:36,260
Does Bernadette ever talk about me?

162
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:37,270
Oh, absolutely.

163
00:07:37,270 --> 00:07:38,400
- She does? - Yeah, sure.

164
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,530
Just yesterday, she asked,

165
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:41,830
"Why is Howard hiding under the table?"

166
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,370
She saw that, huh?

167
00:07:44,370 --> 00:07:45,410
Oh, no, not at first.

168
00:07:45,410 --> 00:07:47,690
Right after I pointed it out.

169
00:07:48,470 --> 00:07:50,080
Let me ask you something else.

170
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,640
Is she seeing anybody?

171
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,320
Oh, not that I know of.

172
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,410
Hey, while we're on the subject,

173
00:07:54,410 --> 00:07:56,070
why did you guys break up anyway?

174
00:07:56,070 --> 00:07:58,090
Oh, I'd rather not say.

175
00:07:58,090 --> 00:08:00,350
Howard, if you want my help, I've got to know what happened.

176
00:08:00,350 --> 00:08:01,790
But it's embarrassing...

177
00:08:01,790 --> 00:08:04,110
Yeah, that's what I'm counting on. Spill.

178
00:08:05,790 --> 00:08:09,100
Okay. Well, you know World of Warcraft?

179
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:10,930
Um, the online game? Sure.

180
00:08:10,930 --> 00:08:11,930
Well, did you know

181
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:16,350
that the characters in the game can have sex with each other?

182
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:20,820
Oh, God. I think I see where this is going.

183
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:24,250
Her name was Glissinda the Troll.

184
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,790
Bernadette walked in on me

185
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:32,420
while we were doing the cyber-nasty under the Bridge of Souls.

186
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:36,240
Oh, you're right. That is so embarrassing.

187
00:08:36,970 --> 00:08:38,330
Would you talk to her?

188
00:08:38,330 --> 00:08:40,520
Bernadette or the troll?

189
00:08:41,270 --> 00:08:42,970
Bernadette. She was so mad at me,

190
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:45,110
she wouldn't even listen to my side of the story.

191
00:08:45,110 --> 00:08:46,370
Well, what was your side?

192
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:49,540
Well, for all we know, Glissinda the Troll wasn't even a real woman.

193
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:53,940
I mean, she could've been a 50-year-old truck driver in New Jersey.

194
00:08:54,690 --> 00:08:57,460
Really? And that didn't make her feel better?

195
00:08:58,710 --> 00:09:01,010
Will you talk to her, see if there's any chance at all

196
00:09:01,010 --> 00:09:02,830
we could get back together?

197
00:09:02,830 --> 00:09:06,040
Oh, gee, Howard, I really don't want to get in the middle of this.

198
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:07,890
No. Why would you?

199
00:09:07,890 --> 00:09:11,690
I'm just another lonely nerd, living with his mother,

200
00:09:11,690 --> 00:09:15,700
trying to find any scrap of happiness he can.

201
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:16,570
You know, maybe to make up for

202
00:09:16,570 --> 00:09:20,290
the fact that his dad left him when he was 11.

203
00:09:20,610 --> 00:09:22,020
Okay, I will think about it.

204
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:24,630
You know, I've always blamed myself

205
00:09:24,630 --> 00:09:26,060
for him leaving.

206
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:29,470
I always thought it was because I wasn't the son he wanted.

207
00:09:29,470 --> 00:09:30,670
Yeah, I said I'd think about it.

208
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:33,310
I wasn't athletic, yeah, I was kind of sickly...

209
00:09:33,310 --> 00:09:36,570
Okay, fine. Look, look, I'm calling her now! See?!

210
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:39,010
Thank you.

211
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:43,540
So anyway, Howard asked Penny to talk to Bernadette,

212
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:44,180
and she did,

213
00:09:44,180 --> 00:09:46,820
and Bernadette agreed to meet him for a cup of coffee.

214
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:48,380
- One question.  - Yeah?

215
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:50,860
Why on earth are you telling me all this?

216
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,970
I don't know.

217
00:09:53,970 --> 00:09:55,600
Sometimes your movements are so lifelike,

218
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:58,250
I forget you're not a real boy.

219
00:10:20,430 --> 00:10:22,420
You said I could buy a desk.

220
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:23,970
This isn't a desk.

221
00:10:23,970 --> 00:10:28,190
This is a... Brobdingnagian monstrosity.

222
00:10:28,390 --> 00:10:32,640
Is that the American idiom for "Giant, big-ass desk"?

223
00:10:33,430 --> 00:10:35,380
It's actually British.

224
00:10:36,230 --> 00:10:37,520
Can you say it again for me?

225
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,320
Brobdingnagian.

226
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,330
One more time?

227
00:10:40,330 --> 00:10:42,350
Brobdingnagian.

228
00:10:42,690 --> 00:10:43,810
Now three times fast?

229
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:45,870
Brobdingnagian, Brobdingna...

230
00:10:49,010 --> 00:10:51,030
How did you even get it in here?

231
00:10:51,030 --> 00:10:54,310
That's for me, Ramon, Julio, Jesus and Rodrigo to know

232
00:10:54,310 --> 00:10:56,910
and you to find out.

233
00:10:57,470 --> 00:10:59,590
All right, you've made your point.

234
00:10:59,590 --> 00:11:02,870
A fine prank, very amusing.

235
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:04,900
Now get it out.

236
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:07,000
- No.  - Yes.

237
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:07,880
- No.  - Yes.

238
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:08,920
- No.  - Yes!

239
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:10,540
I have three brothers and two sisters, Sheldon--

240
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:12,720
I can do this all day.

241
00:11:13,270 --> 00:11:15,580
All right, if you're not going to remove it,

242
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:17,090
I'll remove it for you.

243
00:11:17,090 --> 00:11:19,240
Knock yourself out.

244
00:11:31,470 --> 00:11:32,860
Help me move my desk.

245
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:33,890
- No.  - Yes.

246
00:11:33,890 --> 00:11:34,860
- No.  - Yes.

247
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,980
No. It's too Brobdingnagian.

248
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:41,560
Why do you even want this here?

249
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:44,910
Its size is completely disproportionate to its purpose.

250
00:11:44,910 --> 00:11:46,880
Well, seeing as its purpose was to piss you off,

251
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:49,260
I'd say it's spot-on.

252
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:53,910
All right, I see what's going on.

253
00:11:53,910 --> 00:11:56,590
This is the opening salvo in what will be

254
00:11:56,590 --> 00:12:00,900
an escalating series of juvenile tit-for-tat exchanges.

255
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:03,120
Well titted.

256
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:04,020
Thank you.

257
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:06,880
Stand by for my upcoming tat.

258
00:12:07,430 --> 00:12:08,570
Hey, Sheldon?

259
00:12:08,570 --> 00:12:09,450
Yes?

260
00:12:09,450 --> 00:12:11,440
No.

261
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,360
See what I did there? I turned it around.

262
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:21,780
Sorry, I had to clock out.

263
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:23,560
Oh, no, that's okay.

264
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:25,550
How have you been?

265
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:28,910
Okay. You know, busy, school, work. You?

